resume.md
handoff.md
node_modules/
.worktrees/
.pi/
# .omo/ is otherwise-ignored scratch state, EXCEPT the three files below, which
# are deliberately tracked, load-bearing fixture content, not disposable
# handoff/resume artifacts: docs/examples/p5-passes.json (the bundled
# prosecution example) references them as its provenance transcript/prompt/
# inputs, and packages/prosecute/test/prosecute-cli.test.mjs exercises that
# exact path. They must stay under .omo/evidence/ specifically (not moved
# elsewhere, e.g. docs/examples/) because packages/prosecute/lib/run.mjs's
# isEvidencePath() enforces that a referenced provenance file living inside
# the worktree lives under .adlc/ or .omo/evidence/ ONLY — a trust-boundary
# check preventing review "evidence" from pointing at an arbitrary,
# potentially-spoofed file elsewhere in the repo. Do not delete these three
# files as "cleanup" (see issue in PR #98's history) without also updating
# docs/examples/p5-passes.json and re-running
# packages/prosecute/test/prosecute-cli.test.mjs.
.omo/*
!.omo/evidence/
.omo/evidence/*
!.omo/evidence/p5-review.txt
!.omo/evidence/p5-prompt.txt
!.omo/evidence/p5-inputs.txt
.adlc/*
!.adlc/tickets.json
!.adlc/tickets.example.json
!.adlc/specs/
!.adlc/tickets/
!.adlc/tickets/**
!.adlc/ticket-archive/
!.adlc/ticket-archive/**
!.adlc/manifest.jsonl
# T-MANIFEST-FOREST segments (spec §4.8): trackable in repos that track evidence,
# same as manifest.jsonl above — Fleet's segmented completion commits these
# (packages/fleet/lib/complete.mjs). The lineage token stays untracked: it is
# branch-local bookkeeping (which segment THIS checkout has open), never
# meant to travel with the commit (spec §7 point 1). `*.lock` (adversarial-
# review finding) is @adlc/core's withLedgerLock advisory lock file — transient,
# unlinked when the critical section exits, but a crashed writer can leave one
# behind with a live owner record. This codebase's locks are never stolen from
# a potentially-live owner (see evidence.test.mjs), so a COMMITTED stale lock
# would deadlock every future writer permanently; it must never be trackable,
# same as `.lineage` itself.
!.adlc/manifest.d/
!.adlc/manifest.d/**
.adlc/manifest.d/.lineage
.adlc/manifest.d/*.lock
# P7 findings ledger (ADR 0014). Tracked like the manifest above so the P5→P7
# bridge survives fleet worktrees and CI and the lesson-foundry gate can run
# against real data. Entries are CURATED PROSE finding records — never raw tool
# dumps or secrets (that standing rule is the basis for tracking it; see the ADR).
!.adlc/findings.jsonl
# P7 distilled defenses. The rest of .adlc/ is runtime evidence, but a lesson is
# a permanent, reviewable defense — it has to reach a PR to be worth anything.
!.adlc/lessons/
!.adlc/lessons/**
.adlc/tickets.lock

# Local env files (may contain secrets, e.g. ATTIO_API_TOKEN)
.env.local
.env*.local

# Impeccable working state: decision-server sessions and local live-mode config
# are per-machine and ephemeral. The design system (DESIGN.md, design.json),
# the surface brief, and the approved comps are tracked deliberately.
apps/docs/.impeccable/questions/
apps/docs/.impeccable/live/
apps/docs/.impeccable/mocks/mobile.html
